## Native selection and composition

Remaining causes found after PR #1573:

1. A selected diagram before empty prose can restart Chromium composition,
   leaving provisional `ni` beside committed `你`. A trace places native focus
   inside the rendered SVG after the first input, before ProseMirror reads the
   DOM. A diagram-only or figure-only document can also lose its native range after
   mouseup while ProseMirror keeps a NodeSelection. Chromium then emits no input
   events. Fix the missing browser input target without per-object event patches.
2. An inline image alone in its paragraph can restart composition even when a
   plain caret is already after it. This reproduces without ProseMirror in static
   contenteditable HTML: an inline-block wrapper containing a block-level image
   box triggers Chromium's restart. An inline-level image box fixes that reduction,
   but the app's hovered chrome introduces another trigger not yet isolated. Fix
   the image/chrome box structure rather than filtering provisional text. Native
   selection projection alone does not fix this case.

Reproduce with real selection plus Chromium `Input.imeSetComposition` updates and
commit. This does not verify Android InputConnection or an operating-system IME.
